  "estimates": "per template and batch kind, the contrast of each batch, read on the order and the times the provider executed it (the instant of each job's queued_at, in integer microseconds) and pooled by inverse variance: base, the raw arm contrast P(s=0 | coin read 1) - P(s=0 | coin read 0); twin, t = (P1 - c) - (P0 - c) = P1 - P0 over the two coin twins of one batch, P the raw P(s=0) of a twin and c = (e10 - e01) / 2 the offset of the batch's own readout-0 and readout-1, which cancels in t; the variance of t sums the arm variances of P1 and P0, a deterministic arm taking the Agresti-Coull interval variance; the twin and base rows enter the pool as the executed_order and base_level rules correct them",
